recommend check-in either -- the carded molt LANDED, GREEN on metal, and `%393`'s repair fell out of the roster's own reds between two hot passes. `%392` is OPEN with its repair named and not taken: a card reading a module head at Door and bound comments at Meter, which is shared machinery every body runs and wants its own lap plus a control proving both poles from both sides. **The sharpest thing this round produced is not its own work:** `%389` fired again, on this seat, against the mitigation it names -- shelf names compared to `xy/main` and found free, and the pier had still spent both numbers and folded the same two rows inside the window. Two rounds, two firings, one of them by a hand giving the habit its best effort. The allocator that reads the anointed remote is the lap I would take next, and it touches tools every body runs, so it is yours to place. Three reds stand at gates: `%374`'s receipt chain, `%360`'s remainder in other lanes, and `commit_message_guard`, which cannot pass on a clone lacking the untracked publisher.
